<title>HONG KONG: Climax Int'l year net down 34.3 percent.</title>
<headline>Climax Int'l year net down 34.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   13.9	 vs  20.5</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.2	  vs  1.3</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  15.97 loss vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    52.60	vs  80.03</p>
<p>    Turnover		     709.53     vs  616.28</p>
<p>    Company name		 Climax International Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  August 28 to September 2</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   September 16</p>
<p>NOTE - Climax International is a paper product manufacturer.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss of HK$9.77 million incurred to reorganise the group from primarily only OEM business to OEM and branded (Easyfil) businesses. The Easyfil Group of companies were formed and commenced operations on October 1, 1996, and made a special payment of HK$6.2 million to Mr Fung Kwong Yan, ex-chairman of the group, who resigned as an executive director on February 1 but remained as a non-exective director.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 2.4 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 1.2 cents) vs 2.6 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368.  http://www.hk97.com</p>
